    "Step 1: Identified the initial downtrend using sequential lower highs (LH) and lower lows (LL) on the 4H XAU/USD chart.",
    "Step 2: Marked each new swing low and swing high, labeling them LL and LH respectively to track market structure progression.",
    "Step 3: Noted that the downtrend persisted as long as price remained below the most recent LH level.",
    "Step 4: Observed a break and close above a prior LH, which invalidated the downtrend and indicated a potential shift to an uptrend."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Market structure is defined by swing highs/lows; a valid trend reversal requires price to break and close beyond the most recent opposing swing point—not just a wick or intrabar breach.",
